# claude_toolkit tracks NO own-org submodule (vasic-digital/*, HelixDevelopment/*):
# constitution, containers, challenges, superspec, llms_verifier (LLMsVerifier)
# and claude_code_router (claude-code-router) live FLAT in the parent project and
# resolve via scripts/resolve_deps.sh (single source of truth). Gate:
# scripts/tests/test_gitmodules_no_ownorg.sh.
#
# DELIBERATE EXCEPTION: the only HTTPS URLs (the third-party submodules). It is
# third-party: go.googlesource.com is the canonical upstream of the Go toolchain;
# no SSH mirror is used elsewhere in the fleet, so none is invented here.
[submodule "submodules/go"]
	path = submodules/go
	url = https://go.googlesource.com/go

# SECOND DELIBERATE EXCEPTION, same rationale as submodules/go above: HTTPS,
# third-party (github.com/ryoppippi/ccusage is not an own-org repo, so it is
# NOT subject to the flat-own-org-dependency policy in helix-deps.yaml), and
# vendored so claude-usage.sh / claude-ccusage-build.sh never depend on
# `npx ccusage@latest` reaching the npm registry at runtime. Built locally by
# scripts/claude-ccusage-build.sh (cargo build of rust/, the package's own
# real implementation — see that script's header for why).
[submodule "submodules/ccusage"]
	path = submodules/ccusage
	url = https://github.com/ryoppippi/ccusage.git
